  "notes": "{濡|ぬ}れる means for something to become wet from contact with water or liquid. It describes the thing that gets wet, not the action of wetting.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{濡|ぬ}らす→濡らす：02386_nurasu⟧ (transitive — to wet something)\n- Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{濡|ぬ}れる (X gets wet)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{濡|ぬ}れて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means \"is wet\" (resulting state), not \"is getting wet.\" This is one of the most common uses.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{雨|あめ}→雨：00583_ame⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{濡|ぬ}れる: to get wet from rain\n- ⟦{汗|あせ}→汗：02173_ase⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{濡|ぬ}れる: to be wet with sweat\n- ⟦びしょ{濡|ぬ}れ→びしょ濡れ：16748_bishonure⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦なる→なる：01970_naru⟧: to get soaking wet\n- {濡|ぬ}れた⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧: wet hair\n\nUSAGE:\nThe particle ⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧ marks the cause (⟦{雨|あめ}→雨：00583_ame⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧) while で marks the means or circumstance (⟦{汗|あせ}→汗：02173_ase⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧).",
